<BaseLayout title="Driving">
  <h1>Driving</h1>
  <p>This section covers normal operation of the third-generation 2021 S60. The T5, T6 and T8 Recharge share many driver controls, but their powertrains behave differently and some displays, selectors and features vary by equipment and market.</p>

  <h2>Before driving</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Adjust the seat, steering wheel, mirrors and climate settings before moving.</li>
    <li>Check that doors and the tailgate are closed and all occupants are properly restrained.</li>
    <li>Review warning messages shown at startup. Do not ignore a message that calls for stopping, reduced speed or immediate service.</li>
    <li>Check tire condition and pressure, especially after a temperature change or wheel/tire service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Automatic transmission</h2>
  <p>The 2021 S60 uses an eight-speed automatic transmission. Gear selection is electronic (shift-by-wire), and the selector hardware differs between versions. The selected position is shown in the driver display. Use the instructions for the selector physically installed in the car rather than copying the shift pattern from a different S60.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Position</th><th>Function</th><th>Important note</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th>P — Park</th><td>Mechanically locks the transmission for parking.</td><td>Select only when stationary. Apply the parking brake as well, especially on an incline.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>R — Reverse</th><td>Used when backing up.</td><td>Bring the vehicle to a complete stop before selecting R.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>N — Neutral</th><td>Disconnects the drive gear selection so the vehicle can roll.</td><td>Apply the parking brake whenever stationary in N.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>D — Drive</th><td>Normal automatic forward driving; the transmission selects gears based on speed and power demand.</td><td>Use for ordinary driving.</td></tr>
    <tr><th>M — Manual</th><td>Allows the driver to request upshifts and downshifts.</td><td>Selector operation varies by the installed shifter. The transmission can downshift automatically if speed is too low for the selected gear.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <p class="note"><strong>Parking reminder:</strong> Volvo warns that selecting P may not be sufficient to hold the car on an incline in every situation. Apply the parking brake before leaving the vehicle.</p>

  <h2>Powertrain behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>T5:</strong> turbocharged gasoline engine. T5 is available with front-wheel drive or mechanical AWD, depending on configuration.</li>
    <li><strong>T6:</strong> turbocharged and supercharged gasoline engine with mechanical AWD.</li>
    <li><strong>T8 Recharge:</strong> plug-in hybrid. The gasoline engine drives the front axle and an electric motor drives the rear axle. Regenerative braking and electric drive add behavior that is not present on T5/T6.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Do not compare fuel use, engine response, braking feel or drivetrain noises between these variants as though they use identical hardware. For T8-specific charging, high-voltage and hybrid-system instructions, use the Recharge owner's information.</p>

  <h2>Drive settings and start/stop</h2>
  <p>Some vehicles have selectable drive settings or Individual settings that adapt items such as steering, powertrain response, braking, suspension, instrument display and start/stop behavior. Availability depends on installed equipment and powertrain. Check the actual center-display menu and owner's manual; do not assume a setting shown in another trim is fitted to the car.</p>

  <h2>Driver assistance</h2>
  <p>Features such as Pilot Assist, adaptive cruise control, BLIS, Lane Keeping Aid and Park Assist are equipment-dependent. They are driver-support systems, not autonomous driving. The driver remains responsible for speed, steering, braking, lane position and observing surrounding traffic.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Pilot Assist uses camera/radar information to help with speed, following distance and steering assistance when the conditions allow.</li>
    <li>Steering assistance depends on the system detecting suitable lane markings. Worn, missing, merging or confusing markings can reduce performance.</li>
    <li>Dirt, ice or snow on sensors can reduce the performance of radar-based features such as BLIS.</li>
    <li>Do not use driver assistance as a substitute for attention, safe following distance or control of the vehicle.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note"><strong>Sensor care:</strong> keep the windshield camera area and external radar/sensor areas clean. After windshield, bumper or sensor-area repairs, confirm whether calibration is required using Volvo service information.</p>

  <h2>Warning messages and unusual behavior</h2>
  <p>Record the exact driver-display wording, symbol, ambient temperature, speed, selected drive mode and what the vehicle was doing when the message appeared. For transmission concerns, note whether the symptom occurs cold or warm, during an upshift/downshift, while reversing or under acceleration. For braking or steering changes, stop safely and do not continue if the vehicle is difficult to control.</p>

